      "stem": "Solve: -3(x + 4) = 6",
      "options": [
        { "id": "a", "text": "x = -6" },
        { "id": "b", "text": "x = 2" },
        { "id": "c", "text": "x = -2" },
        { "id": "d", "text": "x = 6" }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "a",
      "explanation": "-3x - 12 = 6. -3x = 18. x = -6. Check: -3(-6 + 4) = -3(-2) = 6."
    },
    {
      "id": "q3",
      "type": "multiple-choice",
      "difficulty": "application",
      "stem": "The angles of a triangle are (3x + 10) degrees, (2x - 5) degrees, and (x + 25) degrees. Find x.",
      "options": [
        { "id": "a", "text": "x = 30" },
        { "id": "b", "text": "x = 25" },
        { "id": "c", "text": "x = 35" },
        { "id": "d", "text": "x = 20" }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "b",
      "explanation": "Angles sum to 180: (3x + 10) + (2x - 5) + (x + 25) = 180. 6x + 30 = 180. 6x = 150. x = 25."
    },
